      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T13:13:44Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, AaveLinearPool creation trace and historical runtime, the pre-transaction aUSDC rate, BlockSec's transaction analysis, verified contract metadata, and the commit-pinned reproduction. Balancer Vault calls onSwap directly at bb-a-USDC pool 0x9210f1204b5a24742eba12f710636d76240df3d0. The crafted sequence first reduces virtual supply and then executes a bb-a-USDC swap whose USDC output rounds to zero while the accounting change inflates the BPT rate cached by the nested boosted pool. No delegatecall originates from the target. Its 17,465-byte runtime has hash 0xa8e951312123e60a23e24ec18bea80c1ca7452a8fd30b36d831ff28f525108d8 at creation block 13799621 and immediately before the exploit. The factory's direct CREATE is therefore the complete code-selection history, giving an age of 53,688,032 seconds. The receipt confirms exact post-flash-loan proceeds of 114,324.73526534493285625 DAI, 253,461.006245 USDT, and 0.970495 aUSDC."
    }
